WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.075 --> 00:00:12.846
They're selling postcards
of the hanging,

00:00:14.247 --> 00:00:17.584
they're painting
the passports brown

00:00:18.785 --> 00:00:22.989
The beauty parlor is
filled with sailors,

00:00:23.957 --> 00:00:26.593
the circus is in town

00:00:28.294 --> 00:00:31.297
Here comes the
blind commissioner,

00:00:32.565 --> 00:00:35.735
they've got him in a trance

00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:40.306
One hand is tied to
the tight-rope walker,

00:00:41.941 --> 00:00:44.911
the other is in his pants

00:00:45.645 --> 00:00:49.649
And the riot squad
they're restless,

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:53.753
they need somewhere to go

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:59.092
As Lady and I look out tonight,

00:00:59.092 --> 00:01:03.096
from Desolation Row

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:11.805
Cinderella, she seems so easy,

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:16.409
"It takes one to know one, "
she smiles

00:01:17.444 --> 00:01:20.780
And puts her hands in
her back pocket

00:01:22.715 --> 00:01:25.285
Bette Davis style

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:29.689
And in comes Romeo,
he's moaning.

00:01:30.657 --> 00:01:34.527
"You Belong to Me I Believe"

00:01:35.061 --> 00:01:40.066
And someone says, "You're in
the wrong place, my friend,

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:43.336
you'd better leave"

00:01:44.070 --> 00:01:48.274
And the only sound that's left

00:01:49.109 --> 00:01:52.445
after the ambulances go

00:01:53.346 --> 00:01:57.484
Is Cinderella sweeping up

00:01:57.484 --> 00:02:01.855
on Desolation Row

00:02:06.159 --> 00:02:10.530
Now the moon is almost hidden,

00:02:11.097 --> 00:02:14.667
the stars are beginning to hide

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:19.706
The fortune telling lady

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:23.476
has even taken all
her things inside

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:27.780
All except for Cain and Abel

00:02:28.615 --> 00:02:32.552
and the hunchback of Notre Dame

00:02:33.653 --> 00:02:37.323
Everybody is making love

00:02:37.323 --> 00:02:40.827
or else expecting rain

00:02:41.895 --> 00:02:45.999
And the Good Samaritan,
he's dressing,

00:02:45.999 --> 00:02:49.802
he's getting ready for the show

00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:55.074
He's going to the
carnival tonight

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:58.845
on Desolation Row

00:03:03.816 --> 00:03:07.387
Ophelia, she's 'neath the window

00:03:08.688 --> 00:03:12.158
for her I feel so afraid

00:03:12.692 --> 00:03:16.196
On her twenty-second birthday

00:03:17.096 --> 00:03:20.867
she already is an old maid

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:25.038
To her, death is quite romantic

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:29.709
she wears an iron vest

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:33.746
Her profession's her religion,

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:38.284
her sin is her lifelessness

00:03:39.185 --> 00:03:44.023
And though her eyes
are fixed upon

00:03:44.023 --> 00:03:47.393
Noah's great rainbow

00:03:48.328 --> 00:03:52.999
She spends her time peeking into

00:03:52.999 --> 00:03:56.002
Desolation Row

00:04:01.441 --> 00:04:05.011
Einstein, disguised
as Robin Hood

00:04:05.612 --> 00:04:08.948
with his memories in a trunk

00:04:10.450 --> 00:04:14.220
Passed this way an hour ago

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:17.790
with his friend, a jealous monk

00:04:18.424 --> 00:04:22.095
Now he looked so
immaculately frightful

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:26.666
as he bummed a cigarette

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:31.437
And he when off
sniffing drainpipes

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:35.875
and reciting the alphabet

00:04:36.442 --> 00:04:40.179
You would not think to
look at him,

00:04:40.179 --> 00:04:45.018
but he was famous long ago

00:04:45.018 --> 00:04:49.022
For playing the electric violin

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:53.092
on Desolation Row

00:04:57.964 --> 00:05:02.001
Dr. Filth, he keeps his world

00:05:02.802 --> 00:05:05.905
inside of a leather cup

00:05:07.106 --> 00:05:11.044
But all his sexless patients,

00:05:11.044 --> 00:05:14.714
they're trying to blow it up

00:05:15.715 --> 00:05:19.319
Now his nurse,
some local loser,

00:05:20.219 --> 00:05:24.057
she's in charge of
the cyanide hole

00:05:24.557 --> 00:05:28.661
And she also keeps the
cards that read,

00:05:28.661 --> 00:05:32.665
"Have Mercy on His Soul"

00:05:33.866 --> 00:05:37.904
They all play on
the penny whistles,

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:41.174
you can hear them blow

00:05:42.075 --> 00:05:47.480
If you lean your head
out far enough from

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:49.916
Desolation Row

00:05:54.887 --> 00:05:59.459
Across the street
they've nailed the curtains,

00:05:59.459 --> 00:06:02.962
they're getting ready
for the feast

00:06:04.163 --> 00:06:08.067
The Phantom of the Opera

00:06:08.067 --> 00:06:12.271
in a perfect image of a priest

00:06:12.538 --> 00:06:16.209
They are spoon feeding Casanova

00:06:17.076 --> 00:06:20.747
to get him to feel more assured

00:06:21.147 --> 00:06:25.518
Then they'll kill him
with self-confidence

00:06:25.518 --> 00:06:28.855
after poisoning him with words

00:06:31.023 --> 00:06:35.862
And the Phantom's shouting
to skinny girls,

00:06:35.862 --> 00:06:39.198
"Get outta here
if you don't know"

00:06:39.899 --> 00:06:45.438
Casanova is just being
punished for going to

00:06:45.438 --> 00:06:47.774
Desolation Row"

00:06:52.879 --> 00:06:56.883
At midnight all the agents

00:06:57.450 --> 00:07:00.987
and the superhuman crew

00:07:01.754 --> 00:07:06.058
Come out and round up everyone

00:07:06.058 --> 00:07:09.295
that knows more than they do

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:14.000
Then they bring them
to the factory

00:07:14.801 --> 00:07:17.804
where the heart-attack machine

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:23.109
Is strapped across
their shoulders

00:07:23.109 --> 00:07:27.113
and then the kerosene

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:31.918
Is brought down from the castles

00:07:31.918 --> 00:07:35.755
by insurance men who go

00:07:36.322 --> 00:07:41.160
Check to see that
nobody is escaping to

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:44.497
Desolation Row

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:51.003
Praise be to Nero's Neptune,

00:07:51.637 --> 00:07:55.308
the Titanic sails at dawn

00:07:56.509 --> 00:07:59.512
Everybody's shouting,

00:08:00.680 --> 00:08:03.516
"Which side are you on?!"

00:08:04.717 --> 00:08:08.221
And Ezra Pound and T.S. Eliot

00:08:09.622 --> 00:08:13.392
fighting in the captain's tower

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:17.663
While calypso singers
laugh at them

00:08:17.663 --> 00:08:21.667
and fishermen hold flowers

00:08:22.435 --> 00:08:26.506
Between the windows of the sea

00:08:26.506 --> 00:08:29.909
where lovely mermaids flow

00:08:31.043 --> 00:08:36.182
And nobody has to think
too much about

00:08:36.182 --> 00:08:38.551
Desolation Row

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:38.077
Yes, I received your
letter yesterday,

00:09:39.045 --> 00:09:43.215
about the time the
doorknob broke

00:09:43.215 --> 00:09:46.919
When you asked me
how I was doing,

00:09:48.087 --> 00:09:51.857
was that some kind of joke

00:09:51.857 --> 00:09:55.528
All these people
that you mention,

00:09:56.162 --> 00:10:00.433
yes, I know them,
they're quite lame

00:10:00.433 --> 00:10:04.770
I had to rearrange their faces

00:10:04.770 --> 00:10:08.107
and give them all another name

00:10:09.609 --> 00:10:13.446
Right now,
I can't read too good,

00:10:13.446 --> 00:10:17.116
don't send me no more letters no

00:10:18.284 --> 00:10:22.455
Not unless you mail them from

00:10:22.455 --> 00:10:25.658
Desolation Row

